WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.788
Start with where the code sits.

2
00:00:01.788 --> 00:00:05.964
The operator steps for retiring
Group Policy are already written,

3
00:00:05.964 --> 00:00:07.938
in this workbook's own guidance.

4
00:00:07.938 --> 00:00:12.333
This code serves two of them:
importing every in-scope GPO into

5
00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:16.901
Group Policy analytics, and creating
the policy library as code.

6
00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:20.475
Two rules shape it, and both
are this workbook's guidance.

7
00:00:20.475 --> 00:00:23.922
One owning policy, and one
owning tool, per setting,

8
00:00:23.922 --> 00:00:27.200
so the library holds only
settings Intune owns.

9
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.590
And build unassigned: the code
creates policies with no assignments,

10
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.362
and assigning them is
a later, reviewed step.

11
00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:36.637
Microsoft Learn sets the stakes.

12
00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:41.562
Its page on importing GPOs into
Group Policy analytics says the tool

13
00:00:41.562 --> 00:00:46.226
is for Windows only, and imports
GPO exports under four megabytes.

14
00:00:46.226 --> 00:00:51.771
Its page on creating a settings catalog
policy from imported GPOs calls the Migrate

15
00:00:51.771 --> 00:00:54.306
step best effort, and says it stops when

16
00:00:54.306 --> 00:00:57.237
two GPOs set one setting
to different values.

17
00:00:57.237 --> 00:01:00.520
And Learn's Microsoft Graph
reference documents the

18
00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.460
migration reports and settings
catalog policies in beta only.
